  "scope": "For every positive natural speed list with exactly four distinct speeds at its minimum 7-adic level and exactly two distinct speeds above that level, the actual real-time loneliness value is at least 1/7. The proof constructs a coprime seed for the two higher speeds, applies the verified four-input filter, derives the normalized unit data from the original list, and transports an explicit folded-residue witness through the common 7-power. Higher levels may be equal and list repeats are permitted. The closure retains the original four-input filtering theorem. This is the 4+2 case; the full six-speed theorem is not claimed.",
